[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Agenda
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirement

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Manual items, iCal (incl. voetbal.nl) and Google Calendar. UIDs: REQ-BE-040 .. 049, REQ-BE-051.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-040
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Manual agenda items
STATEMENT: >>>
Agenda managers shall be able to create, edit and delete agenda items with a title, date, optional start and end time and the repeat options of REQ-BE-031.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-041
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: iCal feeds
STATEMENT: >>>
A person shall be able to subscribe to iCal feeds (HTTPS or webcal URL) with a label, sync interval (15 minutes, 1 hour or 1 day), title prefix, colour and the choice to show times. The backend shall import the feeds in the background, honouring each feed's interval, including repeating events.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-044
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Recognise voetbal.nl feeds
STATEMENT: >>>
When an iCal feed is added or synchronised, the backend shall recognise whether it is a voetbal.nl feed: the calendar name (X-WR-CALNAME) or the event organiser names Voetbal.nl. Only for voetbal.nl feeds the feed settings in the web admin (own profile and user admin) shall show the options of REQ-BE-045, REQ-BE-046, REQ-BE-047 and REQ-BE-048.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The feeds are served by data.sportlink.com (webcal or https, with a personal token), which also serves other sports, so the URL alone does not tell it is football.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-041

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-045
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Home/away mode
STATEMENT: >>>
A voetbal.nl feed shall have a home/away mode, enabled by default for new feeds. When it is enabled, a match is shown with the title 'Voetbal thuis tegen <opponent>' or 'Voetbal uit tegen <opponent>'. When it is disabled, or for an item that is not a match of the own team (for example a training or a match without the own team), the title from the feed is shown unchanged. The feed prefix still applies.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Feed titles like "VV 't Dorp MO15-2-FC Voorbeeld MO15-4" are long and hard to read on the wall tablet; what matters is home or away and against whom.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Titles are shaped when shown, not when imported, so changing the mode or the team name takes effect immediately on all clients without a re-sync.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-044

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-046
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Own team
STATEMENT: >>>
A voetbal.nl feed shall have an 'own team' text field, editable in the feed settings. When the feed is recognised as a voetbal.nl feed and the field is empty, the backend shall fill it with the team name that occurs in the most match titles of the feed. A match title has the form '<home team>-<away team>'; it is a home match when it starts with the own team followed by '-', and an away match when it ends with '-' followed by the own team. The opponent is the rest of the title. A title that matches neither is not a match of the own team.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Team names contain hyphens themselves (e.g. 'VV 't Dorp MO15-2-FC Voorbeeld MO15-4'), so titles cannot simply be split on '-': every split is a candidate and the name found in the most titles wins (the longest one when several are equally common). Once set, the field is never overwritten by the backend.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-044

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-047
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Referee compact mode
STATEMENT: >>>
A voetbal.nl feed shall have a 'Scheidsrechter compact' switch, off by default. When it is on, an item whose title contains the word 'scheidsrechter' (case-insensitive) is shown with the title 'Fluiten <home team>'. The home team is taken from the match in the title (the text after the word 'scheidsrechter' and any following punctuation): it is the part before the '-' that separates the two teams, which is the first '-' that directly follows a digit and is not followed by a digit. For 'Scheidsrechter, FC Club JO15-1-SV Other JO15-2' the home team is 'FC Club JO15-1'. When no home team can be found, the title from the feed is shown unchanged. Items without the word 'scheidsrechter' follow REQ-BE-045. The feed prefix still applies.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Referee duties are listed as 'Scheidsrechter, <home team>-<away team>'; only which match at the own club has to be refereed matters.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Like REQ-BE-045, the title is shaped when shown, so switching takes effect immediately without a re-sync.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-044

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-048
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Club
STATEMENT: >>>
A voetbal.nl feed shall have a 'Club' text field, shown in the feed settings only while the referee compact mode (REQ-BE-047) is on. When the field is empty, the backend shall suggest the own team (REQ-BE-046) without its last word when that word contains a digit (the team code), e.g. 'FC Club' for 'FC Club JO15-1'; the user can edit it. In referee compact mode, a home team that starts with the club followed by a space is shown without the club: 'Fluiten FC Club JO15-1' becomes 'Fluiten JO15-1'. An empty club removes nothing.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-047

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-049
STATUS: Active
TITLE: voetbal.nl items have only a start time
STATEMENT: >>>
For a voetbal.nl feed the backend shall import only the start time of each item; the end time stays empty. This applies to matches, referee duties and all other items of the feed.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Existing items lose their end time on the next synchronisation of the feed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-044

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-051
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Referee duty replaces the same match
STATEMENT: >>>
When importing a voetbal.nl feed, the backend shall detect a match that occurs both as a normal item and as a referee duty: two items with the same start (date and time) where the referee duty's title, without the word 'scheidsrechter' and the punctuation that follows it, equals the normal item's title (case-insensitive, ignoring surrounding whitespace). For example 'FC Club JO15-1-SV Other JO15-2' and 'Scheidsrechter, FC Club JO15-1-SV Other JO15-2' on the same day at 10:00. Only the referee duty shall be imported. This applies whether or not the referee compact mode (REQ-BE-047) is on. Items that differ in start or title are all imported.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
When a person both plays in and referees the same match, voetbal.nl lists it twice; on the wall tablet it should show once, as the referee duty.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-044

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-042
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Google Calendar
STATEMENT: >>>
Once an administrator has configured OAuth credentials, a person shall be able to connect their Google account, choose which calendars to import and filter events by colour. The backend shall sync the chosen calendars about every 10 minutes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-043
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Imported items are read-only
STATEMENT: >>>
Agenda items imported from iCal or Google shall not be editable through Buddyplan (HTTP 403).
<<<
